-- title:
--   Saturation of the toric torsion tower of J₀(N₀p)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $A$ lies over $p$). Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $N_0$, $p$, $A$ — a structure morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the base, compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over the base with a relative group law, and bijections of $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbf{Q}})$ and of the level-$N_0$ points over the residue field of $A$ with the corresponding sections — and assume `Λ.IsJacobian`, the conjunction asserting that $\Lambda.f$ carries the abelian-scheme property bundle, that the group law is commutative, that both point parametrisations are additive, that the generic parametrisation is Galois-equivariant, that reduction of points agrees modulo the uniformiser when the relevant inputs hold, and that every Hecke operator is realised by an endomorphism over the base. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, and let $m \mid m'$ with $m' > 0$. Then $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m = O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m' \sqcap \mathrm{jZeroTorsion}\,(N_0 p)\,m$, an equality of additive subgroups of $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbf{Q}})$, where $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,k$ is the subgroup generated by the range of the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,k$ for $k > 0$ (and $\bot$ for $k = 0$), and $\mathrm{jZeroTorsion}\,(N_0 p)\,m$ is the $m$-torsion subgroup.
--
--   This expresses the saturation of the toric part of the torsion in the level-$N_0p$ Néron object at $p$: the toric $m$-torsion is cut out of the toric $m'$-torsion by the $m$-torsion condition, as it would be for the $m$-torsion of a single torus $\mathbf{G}_m^t$ over the base. It is proved from the cardinality count `natCard_toricPts` together with `toricPts_le_finPts`, and feeds the construction of the at-$p$ Néron datum used further along in the level-lowering argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_toricPts_eq_inf.lean

